<header><p class="st-kicker">tribal confederation · Arabia and the Gulf</p><h1 class="st-title">State of Dathina</h1><p class="st-meta">1944 CE – 1967 CE (approx.) · capital Mudiyah</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A tribal territory of the Aden hinterland without a ruling family, governed by a council under British advice from 1944.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Dathina was a district inland from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gulf-of-aden">Gulf of Aden</a> inhabited by tribes who recognised no sultan or sheikh. In 1944 British officials organised it as a state governed by a tribal council, with its centre at Mudiyah, so that it could be brought into the system of protected states.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Unlike its neighbours, Dathina had no hereditary ruler; a council of tribal representatives chose its head. Its people lived from farming and herding in the valleys. As part of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/aden-protectorate">Western Aden Protectorate</a> it joined the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/federation-of-arab-emirates-of-the-south">Federation of Arab Emirates of the South</a> in 1960.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Dathina remained a member of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/federation-of-south-arabia">Federation of South Arabia</a> until 1967, when the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/national-liberation-front-south-yemen">National Liberation Front</a> took over and the territory was incorporated into <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/south-yemen">South Yemen</a>.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="tribal confederation, 1944 CE – 1967 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><ellipse cx="44" cy="56" rx="16" ry="24"/><path d="M44 34 V78"/><path d="M68 20 V84"/><path d="M68 20 L63 30 H73 Z"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">tribal confederation</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Arabia and the Gulf</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:98.39%;width:1.20%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1944 CE – 1967 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>tribal confederation</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Mudiyah</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Sunni Islam</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Arabic</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/yemen">Yemen</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Dathina</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1956&amp;focus=state-of-dathina" aria-label="State of Dathina on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5942 1659 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where State of Dathina lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M6262 1915L6295 1853M6262 1915L6313 1863M6262 1915L6236 1957"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M6295 1853h0M6313 1863h0M6236 1957h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M6262 1915h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M6262 1915h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Mudiyah. <a href="/atlas?year=1956&amp;focus=state-of-dathina">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
